// ==============================================================================
// File: tests/test4_complex_tac.toy
// Purpose: Test deeply nested expressions and Three-Address Code (TAC) flattening.
//
// What it Tests:
//  - Deeply nested arithmetic formula: p * (1 + (r / 100) * t)
//  - Validates post-order AST traversal to emit linear temporary variables:
//      t1 = r / 100
//      t2 = t1 * t
//      t3 = 1 + t2
//      t4 = p * t3
//      temp_calc = t4
//  - Verifies that complex expression trees flatten into sequential instructions.
// ==============================================================================

// Calculate compound interest variables (mock formula)
p = 1000;
r = 5;
t = 10;
temp_calc = p * (1 + (r / 100) * t);
print(temp_calc);
